2025-11-08 04:27:52,574 | INFO | ai-engine.scorer | Actual: Step-by-Step Guide: How to Get an Emirates ID  The Emirates ID is a mandatory identification card for all UAE citizens and residents. It is essential for accessing government services, opening bank accounts, signing contracts, and many daily activities in the UAE. Below is a clear, step-by-step guide to obtaining your Emirates ID:  1. Ensure You Have a Valid UAE Residence Visa   You must have a valid UAE residence visa before applying for an Emirates ID. This is a strict requirement for expatriates1.  2. Prepare Required Documents  The documents you need may vary depending on your nationality and age, but generally include:   Original passport  Valid UAE residence visa (for expatriates)  Birth certificate (for children)  Passport-sized photos (as per specifications)  Supporting documents for special categories (e.g., GCC nationals, newborns)4.  3. Submit Your Application  You have two main options:   Online:  Apply through the official ICP (Federal Authority for Identity, Citizenship, Customs & Port Security) website or mobile app.  Typing Centre:  Visit an accredited typing centre, where staff will help you fill out the application and collect your documents13.  4. Pay the Application Fee   Fees vary depending on the validity period and applicant category.  Payment can be made online or at the typing centre.  5. Biometric Data Collection   After submitting your application, you will receive instructions to visit an ICP service centre.  At the centre, your fingerprints and photograph will be taken13.  6. Application Processing   Once your biometric data is collected, your application will be processed.  You will receive an SMS notification about the status of your application and when your Emirates ID is ready for collection3.  7. Collect Your Emirates ID   You can collect your Emirates ID from the designated Emirates Post office, or it may be delivered to your registered address, depending on your selection during the application3.  8. Track Your Application (Optional)   You can track the status of your Emirates ID application online via the ICP website or through the typing centre13.  Additional Notes   Urgent Service:  UAE and GCC nationals can use the “Fawri” urgent service to get an Emirates ID within 24 hours for an additional fee. Expatriates can use this only for replacement, not for new issuance1.  Renewal:  Emirates IDs must be renewed before expiry (within 30 days after expiry to avoid fines)1.  Lost or Damaged Card:  Report immediately to the ICP and apply for a replacement1.  References  1: Official UAE Government Guide – Emirates ID Application Process 
2: ICP Official Services Portal 
3: First Abu Dhabi Bank Expat Guide – Emirates ID Steps 
4: Shuraa – Emirates ID Requirements & Documents   If you need more details about specific document requirements or have a unique situation (such as for newborns or GCC nationals), please let me know!    Sources  Ask  Explain
