2025-11-08 11:54:39,402 | INFO | ai-engine.scorer | Actual: Step-by-Step Guide: How to Get an Emirates ID  The Emirates ID is a mandatory identification card for all UAE citizens and residents. It is essential for accessing government services, opening bank accounts, signing contracts, and many other daily activities in the UAE. Below is a clear, step-by-step guide to obtaining your Emirates ID:  1. Ensure You Have a Valid UAE Residence Visa   You must have a valid UAE residence visa before you can apply for an Emirates ID. This is a strict requirement for expatriates1.  2. Prepare the Required Documents  The documents you need may vary depending on your nationality and age, but generally include:   Original passport  Valid UAE residence visa  Passport-sized photographs  Birth certificate (for children)  Supporting documents as required (e.g., sponsor’s documents for dependents)4.  3. Submit Your Application  You have two main options:   Online:  Apply through the Federal Authority for Identity, Citizenship, Customs & Port Security (ICP) website or mobile app.  Typing Centre:  Visit an accredited typing centre, where staff will help you fill out the application form and collect your documents13.  4. Pay the Application Fee   Pay the required fee at the typing centre or online. The fee varies depending on the validity period of your visa and the type of application3.  5. Biometric Data Collection   After submitting your application, you will be notified to visit an ICP service centre to provide your biometric data (fingerprints and photograph). This step is mandatory for first-time applicants and some renewals13.  6. Application Processing   Once your application is processed, you will receive an SMS notification about the status and collection details3.  7. Collect Your Emirates ID   You can collect your Emirates ID from the designated Emirates Post office or have it delivered to your registered address, depending on your selection during the application3.  8. Track Your Application   You may track the status of your Emirates ID application online through the ICP website or at the typing centre where you applied13.  9. Urgent Service (Optional)   If you need your Emirates ID urgently, the ICP offers a ‘Fawri’ service for UAE and GCC nationals, issuing the card within 24 hours for an additional fee. Expatriate residents can use this service only for replacement, not for new issuance1.  Important Notes   Always carry your Emirates ID with you, as it is a legal requirement.  Report any loss or damage of your Emirates ID immediately to the ICP.  Update your Emirates ID details with the ICP if your personal information changes.  References  1: UAE Government Official Portal – Emirates ID Application Process 
